-- title:
--   Existence of a separating transcendental over a perfect field
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $F$ be fields with $K$ perfect and $F$ a $K$-algebra, and let $x \in F$ be transcendental over $K$ (i.e. $x$ is not a root of any nonzero polynomial over $K$) and such that $F$ is finite-dimensional as a module over the intermediate field $K(x)$ generated by $\{x\}$ inside $F$. Then there exists $t \in F$ with three properties: $t$ is transcendental over $K$; $F$ is finite-dimensional over the intermediate field $K(t)$ generated by $\{t\}$; and the extension $F/K(t)$ is separable, in the sense of the `Algebra.IsSeparable` predicate, namely every element of $F$ has separable minimal polynomial over $K(t)$. Thus an algebraic function field of one variable over a perfect field, presented by one transcendental generator $x$ with $[F:K(x)] < \infty$, admits a separating transcendental element.
--
--   This is F. K. Schmidt's theorem that a one-variable algebraic function field over a perfect constant field is separably generated; no hypothesis on the exact constant field of $F$ beyond perfectness of $K$ is made. It underpins the curve-theoretic part of the development, being used for instance in the results on places, regular prolongations and the degree-zero Picard group of a curve.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_exists_separating_transcendental_of_perfectField.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

theorem AlgebraicCurve.exists_separating_transcendental_of_perfectField
    {K F : Type*} [Field K] [Field F] [Algebra K F] [PerfectField K]
    {x : F} (htr : Transcendental K x)
    (hfd : FiniteDimensional (IntermediateField.adjoin K ({x} : Set F)) F) :
    ∃ t : F, Transcendental K t ∧
      FiniteDimensional (IntermediateField.adjoin K ({t} : Set F)) F ∧
      Algebra.IsSeparable (IntermediateField.adjoin K ({t} : Set F)) F := by sorry
